    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0862" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">458.11 Dexter and Carpenter/194: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden (Steinhardt) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-09-30T13:00:00+01:00">September 30,
                            1933—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—9:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. I have just received a check of the Swedish Riksbank drawn on National City
                    Bank of New York City for $150,000 payable to Haight, Smith, Griffen and Deming,
                    attorneys for Dexter and Carpenter, Incorporated.</p>
                <p>I am sending check to the Department by registered mail today via the steamship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Ile de France</hi> due New York October 10th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
